# Copied verbatim from trinodb/trino:483's own /etc/trino/jvm.config, with two
# numbers changed. Copied rather than written, because the flags below are not
# ones you can derive: -agentpath libjvmkill is what turns an OOM into a clean
# process death instead of a hung coordinator, and dropping any of the
# -XX:Per*RecompilationCutoff / jdk.attach lines silently changes how the JIT
# and the JMX agent behave. Regenerate with:
#
#     docker run --rm --entrypoint cat trinodb/trino:483 /etc/trino/jvm.config
#
# What changed, and why -- this is the ADR-004 #8 arithmetic again, in a
# friendlier form. Trino's image is genuinely cgroup-aware: MaxRAMPercentage
# reads the container limit rather than host RAM, so unlike Flink (ADR-004 #8)
# and kafka-ui, this JVM does not need a hardcoded -Xmx to avoid sizing itself
# off the host. What it does need is a percentage that leaves room for the
# NON-heap regions, and the stock 80% does not:
#
#     80% of the 1024m mem_limit  = 819m heap
#     + ReservedCodeCacheSize     = 256m
#                                 = 1075m, i.e. over the cgroup before
#                                   metaspace or a single thread stack
#
# The code cache is reserved virtual address space and is committed lazily, so
# this does not fail immediately -- it fails later, under load, as an OOM kill
# that looks like a query problem. 60% + a 128m code cache leaves ~614m of heap
# and ~250m of everything else inside 1024m.
#
# config.properties then has to fit inside that heap: query.max-memory-per-node
# (256MB) + memory.heap-headroom-per-node (192MB) = 448 of 614. Trino validates
# that at startup and refuses to start if it does not hold.
-server
-agentpath:/usr/lib/trino/bin/libjvmkill.so
-XX:InitialRAMPercentage=60
-XX:MaxRAMPercentage=60
-XX:G1HeapRegionSize=32M
-XX:+ExplicitGCInvokesConcurrent
-XX:+HeapDumpOnOutOfMemoryError
-XX:+ExitOnOutOfMemoryError
-XX:-OmitStackTraceInFastThrow
-XX:ReservedCodeCacheSize=128M
-XX:PerMethodRecompilationCutoff=10000
-XX:PerBytecodeRecompilationCutoff=10000
-Djdk.attach.allowAttachSelf=true
-Djdk.nio.maxCachedBufferSize=2000000
